    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d877">

                <pb facs="0697" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.9312/3.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The request of the Chinese chargé d’affaires at Mexico City, as reported in your
                    telegram of the 8th instant, was communicated to the <pb facs="0698" n="616"
                        xml:id="pg616"/> Department of Commerce and Labor, and that department has
                    sent the following instruction to the immigration inspector at El Paso: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In case attack upon Juárez permit Chinese enter El Paso under hest
                            possible arrangements to insure prompt return on cessation hostilities
                            there.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
